— Records.
It is the function of the Traffic Engineer under
the supervision of the Director of Transportation
to keep records of:
A. Traffic collisions;
B. Traffic volume;
C. Traffic-control devices;
D. Street curb space utilization.
(Ord. 118409 § 16, 1996: Ord. 108200,
§ 2(11.16.200), 1979.)

Special zones
Consistent with Section 11.23.420, the Traffic
Engineer is authorized under the supervision of
the Director of Transportation to:
A. Determine the location of and establish stage zones and bus zones;
B. Determine the location of and establish truck load and commercial load zones where
practicable, when upon investigation it appears
that there are no alley entrances or other similar
means of approach to buildings or property and
that congested traffic conditions require such zones
for the purpose of loading or unloading, and in each case to fix the hours during which such
zones shall be maintained open for the purpose
for which the same are intended;
C. Determine the location of and establish passenger load zones and in each case to fix
the hours during which such zones shall be maintained open for the purpose for which the same
are intended;
D. Determine the location of and establish taxicab, pedicab and other for-hire car stands;
E. Determine the location of and establish car sharing zones;
F. Determine the location of and establish pedestrian zones;
G. Determine the location of and establish food vehicle zones and vending zones;
H. Determine the location of and establish other special zones for the purpose and in
accordance with the criteria specified in this Section 11.16.280;
I. Make surveys and recommendations
with respect to the Stadium Event Restricted
Parking Zone, process applications for parking in
the zone, issue decals or other authorizations for
parking, and delegate to the University of Washington or deputize its staff to receive applications
and deliver permits.
